    },
    {
      "la": "VERS. 3.--",
      "en": "VERS. 3.--",
      "column": "728c",
      "chunk": 1
    },
    {
      "la": "etc. Christus imminente mortis articulo coepit pavere et taedere, non diabolum, sed mortem, quae invidia diaboli intravit in orbem, naturali carnis fragilitate perhorrescens; unde",
      "en": "…n the moment of death was at hand, began to fear and to be heavy, dreading with the natural frailty of the flesh not the devil, but death, which entered into the world by the envy of the devil; whence",
      "column": "728c",
      "chunk": 1
    },
    {
      "la": "VERS. 4.--",
      "en": "VERS. 4.--",
      "column": "728c",
      "chunk": 1
    },
    {
      "la": "",
      "en": "",
      "column": "728d",
      "chunk": 1
    },
    {
      "la": "VERS. 5.--",
      "en": "VERS. 5.--",
      "column": "728d",
      "chunk": 1
    },
    {
      "la": "…inus piscem exenteravit, cum nequitiam diaboli latius sanctis aperuit: et quasi arcana insidiarum ejus reseravit. Reposuit sibi cor ejus, quia calliditatem ejus in Scripturis indicavit, de quo dicitur",
      "en": "…evil more widely to the saints: and, as it were, unlocked the secret things of his snares. He laid up for himself his heart, because he pointed out his craftiness in the Scriptures, of whom it is said",
      "column": "729a",
      "chunk": 1
    },
    {
      "la": "et alibi",
      "en": "and elsewhere",
